# Line endings.
#
# Everything below is read by a Unix runtime — a shell, Docker, Caddy — and a
# CRLF checkout breaks it in ways that are hard to attribute. `#!/bin/sh\r` is
# not a shebang: the kernel looks for an interpreter whose name ends in a
# carriage return and reports "no such file or directory" about a file that is
# plainly there. Inside a script, a heredoc's body carries the `\r` into the
# variables it feeds, so a comparison against clean data silently fails.
#
# That is not hypothetical here. Without this file, a Windows checkout produced
# CRLF for all twelve shell scripts, and `deploy/check.sh` reported two
# documentation checks as failing because the patterns it extracted through a
# heredoc each carried a trailing `\r` — a local run answering a different
# question from the one CI answers, which is exactly what CLAUDE.md warns
# about. The image was never affected because CI builds it on Linux; a build
# from a Windows working copy would have shipped a container that cannot start.
*.sh text eol=lf
deploy/bin/* text eol=lf
docker/entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
docker/Caddyfile text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# The knowledge-library fixtures, and the same reasoning one level down.
#
# Git decides text-versus-binary by looking for a NUL byte, and today all four
# of these formats have one — so nothing is broken. But three of them also
# carry `\r\n` *inside* their compressed streams, and the day a small enough
# file has no NUL, an autocrlf checkout would rewrite those two bytes and
# corrupt it: a PDF's cross-reference offsets all shift, and the reader reports
# "not a PDF" about a file that was committed intact. Saying `binary` here
# costs nothing and removes the guess.
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pptx binary

# And their text siblings pinned to LF, so a fixture is the same bytes on every
# machine as the ones the generator wrote — a test that asserts an exact
# extraction should not depend on who checked it out.
apps/api/src/learning/extract/fixtures/*.csv text eol=lf
apps/api/src/learning/extract/fixtures/*.html text eol=lf
apps/api/src/learning/extract/fixtures/*.md text eol=lf
apps/api/src/learning/extract/fixtures/*.tex text eol=lf
